{"base_rate":0.2993288590604027,"brier":0.07655181208053691,"bss":0.6350001761077608,"bss_hi":0.7025353636358329,"bss_lo":0.5679565748320653,"chart":{"base":[450.1,66.9],"fp":[203.1,333.4],"lead":"62,231.7 272,228.6 482,197.7 692,157.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.64 — higher than 98% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +5pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 32% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 98% → rained 91%"},"rel":"71.1,455.3 361.4,252.8 679.1,71.4"},"country":"ME","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.024308724832214752,"ess":299.78120928088344,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Podgorica</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Podgorica rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>91%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 745 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPODGORICA, 1.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.64, ranked 3 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(2&ndash;7) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>346</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>97</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>65%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>91%</b></td><td class='num'>150</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Podgorica</b> <span class=\"muted\">ME</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.64</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>2&ndash;7\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>745 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Podgorica &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Podgorica\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 81.35670103092784,336.96907216494844 162.43,234.43243243243242 286.7838461538461,111.33333333333331 404.7548,18.0 404.7548,34.98666666666668 286.7838461538461,186.0 162.43,313.1351351351351 81.35670103092784,374.49484536082474 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"273.04429530201344\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"273.04429530201344\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,380.94797687861274 81.35670103092784,344.4742268041237 162.43,259.02702702702703 286.7838461538461,148.66666666666666 404.7548,49.54666666666668\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 346 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"380.94797687861274\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 97 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"81.35670103092784\" cy=\"344.4742268041237\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"162.43\" cy=\"259.02702702702703\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 65%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"286.7838461538461\" cy=\"148.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 91% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 150 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.7548\" cy=\"49.54666666666668\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Podgorica the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.72) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.36).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>0.364</td><td class='num'>2.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.612</td><td class='num'>1.6%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>165</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.627</td><td class='num'>5.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.724</td><td class='num'>2.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":42.44124,"lon":19.26309,"n":745,"n_cities":134,"name":"Podgorica","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":346,"obs":0.002890173410404624,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.06597938144329897,"n":97,"obs":0.10309278350515463,"sig":false},{"hi":0.48,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.29500000000000004,"n":74,"obs":0.33783783783783783,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.48,"mean":0.6462820512820512,"n":78,"obs":0.6410256410256411,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9795333333333334,"n":150,"obs":0.9133333333333333,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.3,"provisional":false,"rank":3,"rank_hi":7.0,"rank_lo":2.0,"reliability":0.0012507590536700126,"resolution":0.13410386188172727,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"podgorica","station":"PODGORICA","timezone":"Europe/Podgorica"}